    "message": "Reuse compiler replies and repair the paid live tests\n\n- Intervention previews now keep accepted compiler replies in\n  runs/<run>/compiler-tape.json (StoredResponseTape). Before, an identical\n  instruction was refused by the ledger's duplicate guard and fell back to\n  the offline parser.\n- The opt-in live tests predated thinking headroom: the model-family test's\n  $0.03 budget could not cover an Opus reservation, and its 96-token output\n  total ignored thinking tokens. Raise that budget to $0.15 and bound each\n  call's output by its own cap. Give the search test two calls of allowance,\n  since a web-search call reserves two sampling passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
